{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"The natural-timing probe bounded the interleaving at zero in 792 deliveries and pointed the open question at the width of the election's read-modify-write rather than at delivery density, since heavier delivery postpones the campaign it is trying to catch. This turn follows that direction with a probe that keeps natural timing but gives the term write a realistic slow-store latency: a store that sleeps before applying the current-term write, the way a fsync on a busy disk behaves. That is an environment property rather than a hook that holds one chosen write open, and it widens the window to the store's write latency, so every heartbeat delivered during that latency is written inside the election's read-modify-write. If window width is what has kept the rate down, falls should appear here with no instrumentation of the write path at all. The reading rule was fixed in advance and is the same one used before: a sampled term below the highest term already adopted is a monotonicity violation, since this implementation only ever writes the current term plus one or an adopted higher term, and the count of such falls per delivery is the result. A second zero would say width is not the limiting factor and would send the question back to the delivery structure, which I recorded along with the direction in the investigation's discriminator and the two saved premises the probe relies on. No interpretation is recorded until the receipt exists. Both files validate and the probe is queued for clean-copy execution; the six witnessed findings, the reproduced regression with its causal control, the two knowledge corrections, and the scoped log-cache negative remain recorded and unaffected.\"}"}}
